     "id": "notes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Purpose.** Find the market-clearing wage by hand: at a trial wage above it households offer more hours than the firm wants; below it, fewer. Then hold the wage above equilibrium with a floor and read unemployment off the gap.\n- **Model.** A view of [Labor Market Supply and Demand Model](note:labor-market-supply-and-demand-model) with no taxes ($\\tau_w = \\tau_f = 0$ fixed): $L^S = 100w$, $L^D = a/w$.\n- **Elements.** Panel `market`: curves `supply`, `demand`; points `eq`, `probe_s` (draggable vertically, bound to `wp`), `probe_d`, `floor_s`, `floor_d`; lines `gap`, `floor`, `unemp_line`. Readouts `w_out`, `L_out`, `excess_out`, `unemp_out`, `emp_out`.\n- **Goal it supports.** `abs(excess) < 1` is met only at $w = 20$ on the 0.5 slider grid."
      }
     ],
     "words": 110,
     "symbols": [
      "$w$",
      "$L$",
